        "original_id": "7555ac44-f18a-5f97-a14b-cf67fdde94d8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Clianthus, Callicoma serratifolia\n- Genera: Clianthus, Callicoma\n- Places: New Zealand, Australia\n- Concepts: Fabaceae, flowering plants, shrubs, small trees, Māori names\n\nFacts:\n- Clianthus is a genus of flowering plants in the legume family Fabaceae.\n- Clianthus is commonly known as kakabeak and as “Kōwhai ngutukākā” in Māori.\n- Clianthus comprises two species of shrubs native to New Zealand.\n- Callicoma is a plant genus that contains one species, Callicoma serratifolia.\n- Callicoma serratifolia is a tall shrub or small tree native to Australia.",
